\ Standalone AOT lint driver: the same bootstrap the `1z lint` subcommand
\ runs through the interpreter, against a fixed fixture, so the compiled
\ tokenize / lint path can be built ahead-of-time. The target path is embedded
\ rather than read from argv.
\
\ Run-and-match test: the runtime-image driver builds and, with ONEZ_STDLIB
\ pointed at the standard library (so the linted file's own `use` imports
\ resolve at runtime), produces output identical to interpreted
\ `1z lint tests/fixtures/lint/unused-import.1z`.
use "lint" ;
use "lint-rules" ;
{ "tests/fixtures/lint/unused-import.1z" } run-lint [ 0 ] [ 1 ] if sys-exit
